    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="0711" n="615" xml:id="pg615"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.51/316: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Price</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Panama</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-06-25T20:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25, 1921—8
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 27—9:20
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>117. Contract referred to in 115<anchor n="12" xml:id="d554-f1"/> and 116
                    returned to International Banking Corporation today approved by the President
                    but with a letter from Secretary of the Treasury canceling from July 1st former
                    order requiring countersignature Fiscal Agent and directing that all funds left
                    with said bank after said date must be considered subject to checking by the
                    sole signature of Secretary of the Treasury.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
